            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-body field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><h3>Halloween Hijinks</h3>
<p>October 25 and 26 from 10 am to 4 pm (final entry by 3 pm)<br>
<strong>Cost: $23.35 per group, plus tax&nbsp;</strong>(maximum of 6 people per group; children under 2 are not counted toward the group total).<br>
<a href="https://anc.ca.apm.activecommunities.com/ottawa/activity/search?locale=en-US&amp;activity_select_param=2&amp;activity_keyword=Halloween%20Hijinks&amp;viewMode=list">Advance registration is required.</a></p>
<p>Celebrate all things silly, fun and a little bit spooky at Cumberland Heritage Village Museum. Pumpkins have taken over the museum! From the scavenger hunt to the witch’s cauldron and beyond, we’ve put a pumpkin twist on all our favourite kid-friendly games and hands-on activities. Even the weekend’s cooking demo and craft have been inspired by everyone’s favourite gourd! Featuring special guests<strong>: Luciano Lu - stilt walker;&nbsp;Chris Pilsworth - magician; Jacky - airbrush temporary tattoo artist; Ottawa Fire Services. </strong>Activities are best suited for children 10 and under. Costumes are encouraged!&nbsp;<span> </span></p>
<p>Admission ($23.35 plus tax) includes entry for up to 6 people (at least one group member in attendance must be an adult over the age of 18). Children under two are not counted toward the group total.&nbsp;</p>
<p>*The Ottawa Valley Live Steamers and Model Engineers will be on site providing complementary demonstrations of their large-scale model locomotives on Sunday, October 27 only. Train demonstrations are weather dependent and may be cancelled without notice in the event of poor conditions.</p>
<h4><strong>Notes</strong></h4>
<ul>
<li>Registration is non-refundable and non-transferable.</li>
<li>Please take careful note of the date and session (morning or afternoon) you registered for. Your registration is valid for the indicated session only.</li>
<li>This program will take place rain or shine. Please dress for the weather as some activity stations will be outdoors.</li>
<li>All reasonable attempts will be made to ensure treats are nut free. However, we cannot guarantee a nut free environment. Please let a staff member know if you have allergy concerns.</li>
<li>The museum grounds include compressed gravel pathways, grass and uneven terrain. If you have questions regarding accessibility, please contact 613-580-2988 or email <a href="mailto:museecumberlandmuseum@ottawa.ca">museecumberlandmuseum@ottawa.ca</a>. <a href="https://ottawa.ca/en/arts-heritage-and-events/museums-and-historic-sites/cumberland-heritage-village-museum#section-bfcdb634-1493-45de-92e2-99811b7f774e">Additional information about accessibility</a> can be found on the museum’s webpage.</li>
</ul>
